S|       1       EXT. LEHIGH RIVER - FALLEN OAK TREE - LATE DAY               1       
N|               MARE advances deeper into the woods. The river is louder and         
N|               angrier out here, the forest primeval. Up ahead, a towering          
N|               old-growth white oak has fallen, impeding her path. She              
N|               scales the massive trunk, climbing between limbs as crooked          
N|               as witch fingers. And she presses on.                                
O|
S|       2       EXT. LEHIGH RIVER - DEEPER IN THE WOODS - LATE DAY           2       
O|
N|               JOHN and BILLY are taking a break from fishing. They’re              
N|               eating ham and cheese sandwiches.                                    
C|                                   BILLY                                            
U|                         Yunno what I think about all the                           
U|                         time? A patch of ice out on Route                          
U|                         18. And cause’a that patch of ice,                         
U|                         my truck slides off the road,                              
U|                         crashes into a tree and kills my                           
U|                         wife and little girl. And ‘cause                           
U|                         they die, I have no one to stay in                         
U|                         my cabin during that family                                
U|                         reunion. So I invite Kenny and                             
U|                         Erin. And one night while they’re                          
U|                         in my cabin, you come in to check                          
U|                         on me. And you an’ her end up                              
U|                         talkin’ all night. And you fall in                         
U|                         love with her. And not long after                          
U|                         that night you put a baby inside                           
U|                         her. And you ask me to help you                            
U|                         keep your secret. You tell me it’ll                        
U|                         ruin your family if it ever gets                           
U|                         out. And so I help. ‘Cause you’re                          
U|                         my older brother. ‘Cause I looked                          
U|                         up to you my whole life. So I pay                          
U|                         her money. I buy her gifts.                                
U|                         Necklaces. Diapers. Anything to                            
U|                         keep your secret.                                          
N|               Wait. What did he just say?                                          
M|               So now we know Billy isn’t DJ’s real father.                         
O|
M|               JOHN IS.                                                             
