U|                         Good evening. I understand that for                        
U|                         some of you seeing me at the                               
U|                         lectern again is uncomfortable.                            
U|                         Many of you have welcomed me back                          
U|                         into the parish while others have                          
U|                         been understandably apprehensive.                          
U|                         It’s taken me eight long months to                         
U|                         gather the courage to stand before                         
U|                         all of you again. But I’ve done a                          
U|                         lot of observing during that time                          
U|                         and I feel as if we’ve finally come                        
U|                         out of a tunnel. Arrived at the                            
U|                         next level of healing. I can sense                         
U|                         a great spirit rising once again                           
U|                         within Easttown. It’s a wondrous                           
U|                         thing... But there are members of                          
U|                         this community that haven’t emerged                        
U|                         with us. Members that have been                            
U|                         ravaged by the terrible events of                          
U|                         this past year. They now find                              
U|                         themselves outside of a circle they                        
U|                         were once a part of. The circle of                         
U|                         this community was once their                              
U|                         life... And it might occur to you                          
U|                         that they deserve to be outside                            
U|                         this circle. That the                                      
U|                         transgressions they’ve committed,                          
U|                         the lies they’ve told, have no                             
U|                         place here. But it is not for us to                        
U|                         decide whether or not they are                             
U|                         deserving. Our job is only to                              
U|                         love... So I urge you to go to                             
U|                         them. They’ll push you away, lock                          
U|                         you out, tell you they’re not                              
U|                         worthy of receiving your mercy.                            
U|                         Don’t let them.                                            
